<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 3 \\ 2 \end{array}\right)}</m>. For each vector, choose whether it is a multiple of <m>\mathbf{a}</m> in the same direction, a multiple in the opposite direction, or not parallel to <m>\mathbf{a}</m>.</p><div>(a) <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -4 \end{array}\right)}</m>: [ same direction as a | opposite direction to a | not parallel to a ]  </div><div>(b) <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -1 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)}</m>: [ same direction as a | opposite direction to a | not parallel to a ]  </div><div>(c) <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 6 \\ 5 \end{array}\right)}</m>: [ same direction as a | opposite direction to a | not parallel to a ]  </div><div>(d) <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 9 \\ 6 \end{array}\right)}</m>: [ same direction as a | opposite direction to a | not parallel to a ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>A vector is parallel to <m>\mathbf{a}</m> when it is a multiple <m>k\mathbf{a}</m>: divide each component by the matching component of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>. If you get the same number k both times, it is <m>k\mathbf{a}</m>; k positive means the same direction, k negative the opposite direction.</p><ul><li>(a) Each component is <m>{-2}</m> times the matching component of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>. <m>{-2}</m> is negative, so the direction is opposite.</li><li>(b) Divide each component by the matching component of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>: you get <m>{-\frac{1}{3}}</m> and <m>{-1}</m>. They are not equal, so this vector is not a multiple of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>.</li><li>(c) Divide each component by the matching component of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>: you get <m>{2}</m> and <m>{\frac{5}{2}}</m>. They are not equal, so this vector is not a multiple of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>.</li><li>(d) Each component is <m>{3}</m> times the matching component of <m>\mathbf{a}</m>. <m>{3}</m> is positive, so the direction is the same.</li></ul></p></solution>
    <answer><p>opposite direction to a</p></answer>
    <answer><p>not parallel to a</p></answer>
    <answer><p>not parallel to a</p></answer>
    <answer><p>same direction as a</p></answer>
</stack-static>